  "findings": [
    "longitudinal differentials match prediction to 0.012 and 0.002 percentage points",
    "all three carry a common -0.14% offset because the true distance is the camera path length, which includes body sway the wheel rotation does not see; being common-mode it cancels in the differential",
    "lateral: the tool reports how much ground a row covers, the prediction was how much larger an object appears, and those are reciprocal. Magnitudes agree to 0.026 and 0.007 percentage points, inside one standard error of 0.058",
    "the optical height shifts 1:1 with the tyre radius in motion as it did at rest (-4.761 and +4.905 mm against a predicted 5), and its spread is unchanged, so the tyre changes the mean and not the dynamics",
    "in-row nonlinearity and the roll-like term are the same in all three, so the tyre does not reach the behaviour inside a row"
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "the cruise spread here is about 6 mm against 2.5 mm on the 100 m run: a 20 m region spends proportionally more of its captured rows near the ramps, and n is about 210 tags rather than 3342",
    "ground truth is used for evaluation only; none of it reaches the stitching optimiser"
  ],
  "turn_speed": "these are the first multi-track runs after the rotation rate went to 0.80 rad/s. Three close handshakes outlasted one control tick across the three runs and none latched Brake."
}
